the battle to control the coyote 19  pandemic in latin america  is underway but is being hindered by  patchy deliveries of the vaccine  and scandals in the government with the  task of organizing the vaccination  programs  the latest to go is the ecuadorian  health minister juan carlos  who admitted ensuring that his family  was given preferential treatment  we have all committed errors this is a  pandemic that has taught us the  importance of recognising them  last month as the vaccines arrived in  ecuador a country one of the highest per  capita death rates in the region  he said they would firstly be given to  the most vulnerable  for the people who are on the front line  medical staff and also people over 65  years old  many of them are still waiting for the  former minister  has fled the country a similar scandal  emerged earlier in peru  when it was revealed that at least two  ministers and a former president  were among nearly 500 people to be  immunized weeks before the rest of the  population  and in argentina a few days later their  health minister genes gonzalez garcia  resigned when it came to light he'd  invited friends and colleagues to  receive what have been called  vip vaccines his replacement carlo  vistotti has since tested positive for  kovite 19  and is self-isolating supplies from a  number of sources continue to arrive  this first batch of nearly 200 000 doses  landing in uruguay  from the chinese cinevac laboratory  and 40 tons of oxygen donated by chile  to peru  where supplies have run dangerously low  [Applause]  but protests against handling of the  pandemic are increasingly common this  one on saturday in buenos aires  if they give it to the president and the  vice president then okay  but they shouldn't vaccinate the  deputies or the ministers that's no good  i've got inside information from  independent media that the pandemic  doesn't exist  it's just tests that have fooled the  whole world  while they're angry with the government  some still believe the pandemics is a  hoax  while others are against the vaccine  whatever else people feel they're  impatient to put the pandemic behind  them  frustrated by the slow pace of the  vaccination programs  confused by contradictory information  and angered by corruption in their  governments  the road towards normality is still  fraught with obstacles  daniel schweiner al jazeera buenos aires
 

